  "notes": "Phase C EXTRACTION for leaf 'pricing' — MetroGraph market research. Extracted 21 pricing_models (covering data visualization, graph databases, low-code platforms, knowledge graphs, vector databases, backends, open-core examples, and workflow automation) from 51 curated pricing sources. 45 pricing_tiers mapped across major competitors. Model types include: seat-based (11), freemium (6), usage-based (6), open-core (3), hybrid (1), flat (1). Billing units: user/month (primary), flat fees, custom, tasks. Free tier prevalence: 18/21 models (86%). Transparency: 15 public, 4 partial, 2 quote-only. Key archetypes covered: (a) BI/Viz: Tableau ($15-75/user/mo seat), Power BI ($0-24/user/mo seat), Metabase (freemium $0-20), Qlik ($24-50 seat), Grafana (freemium $0-299 flat), Looker Studio (free); (b) Low-code: Retool ($10-50 seat), Budibase ($0-15 seat), Appsmith ($0-25 seat); (c) Databases: Airtable ($0-45 seat), Notion ($0-18 seat); (d) Knowledge graphs: Obsidian (hybrid $0-10/mo), Roam ($15/mo flat); (e) Graph DBs: Neo4j (open-core community free, custom enterprise); (f) DevTools: GitLab (open-core $0-99 seat), Elasticsearch (open-core $0-180 flat); (g) Automation: Zapier (usage $0-69/mo); (h) Backend: Supabase ($0-599 flat usage), Firebase ($0-custom usage); (i) Vector DBs: Pinecone (usage ~$70/mo partial transparency), Weaviate (usage ~$135/mo partial), Qdrant (usage ~$65/mo public). All source_ids cited for traceability to T0-T3 source corpus (65 unique URLs). MetroGraph positioning: Enterprise graph visualization bridging data engineer and business analyst personas aligns with: (1) seat-based precedent (Tableau, Power BI dominance in $14-75 range), (2) freemium conversion patterns (2-5% free-to-paid, hybrid 65% PLG adoption), (3) vertical SaaS growth (18-32% annual, 85% usage-based adoption), (4) graph database ecosystem maturation (Neo4j + emerging open-source competition)"
